provenance.prompt:
Use the supplied Nova Stitch gameplay sprite only as an identity and style reference. Create an original 1536×1024 transparent RGBA JAMVERSE '96 sheet with exactly eight separate full-body Nova Stitch right-handed layup poses in a four-column by two-row grid, row-major. Same scale, facing, camera, body proportions and color palette in all cells. No scene, floor, court, shadows, glow, borders, text, numbers, ball, hoop, prop, teammate or opponent.

Nova is a young athletic fair-tan woman with long curly teal hair in a high ponytail, an individual face, teal jersey and shorts with purple/black trim, black knee pads, teal-black shoes and wristbands. Preserve this exact human identity, hair, uniform and shoes. Both hands remain empty; basketball is separately rendered and is never drawn in poses.

Action: right-facing running approach, gather the separate ball, plant, jump for a one-handed right-hand layup toward image-right, then land and recover. Eight connected unique poses:
0 controlled rightward running approach, arms swing naturally;
1 gather hands at waist while taking the last running step;
2 TAKEOFF at tick2: plant lead foot and lift opposite knee;
3 rise forward, shooting hand and elbow lift above shoulder;
4 single RELEASE at tick10: leap toward right, right arm fully extended, open hand flicks upward;
5 follow through at peak with hand high and eyes toward the rim;
6 descend, torso stays upright, arms begin to lower;
7 land under control with knees flexed and return to a balanced stance.
The hand is empty after frame4; no ball is drawn. Keep human limbs and complete hair/shoes visible, with naturally connected motion. Don’t let the ponytail touch adjacent cells.

Match the tiny gameplay sprite reference with crisp limited-palette 1990s arcade pixel art and chunky dark pixel outlines, not painterly, photoreal, 3D, glossy or anime. Background and cell gutters must have true alpha zero and no matte, shadow or checkerboard. Return only the sprite sheet.
